  <h2>Find the source first</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Clues</th><th>Usual fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Rain and surface water</td><td>Water after storms, worst near downspouts or low corners</td><td>Extend downspouts, clean gutters, regrade soil away from the house</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Groundwater</td><td>Water seeping through walls or up through the floor in wet seasons; high water table</td><td>Perimeter drain and sump pump, then a vapor barrier</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plumbing leaks</td><td>Wet spot under a bathroom, kitchen or water heater; water year-round</td><td>Repair the pipe, dry the area, replace wet insulation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ductwork</td><td>Wet insulation and condensation on ducts in summer; disconnected duct</td><td>Seal and insulate ducts, reconnect loose runs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Summer condensation</td><td>Damp joists and dripping pipes in humid weather with no rain</td><td>Ground vapor barrier, air sealing, and dehumidification or conditioning</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
